Overlay patch 0056: ROUND THE TILE SIZE, DON'T TRUNCATE IT.
`vendor/Shipwright/libultraship/src/fast/interpreter.cpp`, LUS at our own pin.

THE SYMPTOM (external report, iPhone 15, 60 Hz, `OoT_Reloaded` HD pack). The
Death Mountain Crater lava and the Water Temple water "jiggle violently" —
the whole texture plane snaps to a slightly larger scale and back, many times
a second. Non-HD (vanilla) textures on the same surfaces are steady.

THE MECHANISM. SoH's frame interpolation emits fractional tile coordinates for
scrolling textures on every RENDERED frame: `Gfx_TwoTexScrollEx` /
`Gfx_TwoTexScrollEnvColorEx` in `soh/src/code/z_rcp.c` bake one
`gDPSetTileSizeInterp` per interpolated frame, and the interpreter stores those
endpoints into `mRdp->texture_tile[].uls/ult/lrs/lrt`, which are FLOATS (see
the `G_SETTILESIZE_INTERP` handler, which memcpy's float words straight into
them). Every place that needs the tile's pixel dimensions then does

    uint32_t tile_w = (uint32_t)((lrs - uls + 4) / 4);

— a C cast, i.e. TRUNCATION. At 60 Hz the port runs 3 interpolated frames per
game frame, so the step is 1/3 of a texel and the float arithmetic lands on
values like 127.9999 / 4 → 31.9999. Truncated that is 31, not 32, on roughly
12% of frames.

WHY ONLY HD PACKS JIGGLE. Upstream LUS `ec194d6b` (#1118, inside our pin) made
HD replacement textures normalize their texcoords against that computed tile
width/height — the `isHd ||` term in the clamp conditions. Vanilla textures
skip the clamp entirely and never see the number. So on the ~12% of frames
where the tile reads 31 instead of 32, an HD texture is scaled by 32/31 in both
axes, and that error is MULTIPLIED by the repeat count across a big lava or
water plane. Hence "violent" on exactly the large scrolling surfaces, and
invisible on small ones.

Upstream tracks this as https://github.com/Kenix3/libultraship/issues/1119 and
the proposed fix there is the same one: round instead of truncate.

THE FIX. `lroundf` of the same float expression at every site that derives tile
dimensions from the float tile fields — five places, found by grepping
`lrs - mRdp->texture_tile[tile].uls + 4`:

  * `ImportTextureRgba16`, `ImportTextureRgba32`, `ImportTextureCI4`,
    `ImportTextureCI8` — the `tile_w`/`tile_h` pyramid/HD clamp gate.
  * the tri/vertex path's `tex_width2[i]` / `tex_height2[i]`, which is what
    actually feeds the HD texcoord normalization per draw.

(The other `lrs`/`lrt` readers — `GfxDpLoadBlock`, `GfxDpLoadTile`, the texrect
and background paths — take integer arguments straight off the display list and
never see a fractional value, so they are untouched.)

Everything is `#ifdef __IOS__` with upstream's exact line kept in the `#else`,
so the macOS build (`scripts/build-oracle.sh`) keeps upstream behaviour byte
for byte and stays a valid comparison point. `math.h` is already included at the
top of the file; no new include is needed.

Patch 0057/0058 fold in upstream's structural fix (`G_SETTILESIZE_LERP`), which
removes most of the fractional traffic at the source. This patch stays anyway:
it is cheap, it is correct on its own, and any other producer of fractional tile
sizes (mods, future interp paths) gets the same protection.

